Kill me!

274
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:01,110
You're no good to me dead.

275
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:03,020
We need you.

276
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:27,340
You don't look like a Theon Greyjoy anymore.

277
00:19:29,110 --> 00:19:30,770
That's a name for a lord.

278
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:33,580
But you're not a lord,

279
00:19:34,390 --> 00:19:35,280
are you?

280
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:39,240
You're just meat.

281
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:44,260
Stinking meat.

282
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:49,140
You reek.

283
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:52,870
Reek!

284
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:55,220
That's a good name for you.

285
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:57,840
What's your name?

286
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:01,440
Theon Greyjoy.

287
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:08,290
What's your name?

288
00:20:11,550 --> 00:20:12,320
Th--

289
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,930
Theon Greyjoy.

290
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:23,400
Please.

291
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:27,850
What is your name?!

292
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:31,110
Reek.

293
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,140
My name is...

294
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,030
Reek.

295
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:07,060
Hodor.

296
00:21:40,510 --> 00:21:42,200
- Don't kill me! - Who are you?

297
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:44,350
- Sam! Sam! - Who are you?!

298
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,770
Gilly. Don't hurt us.

299
00:21:48,490 --> 00:21:49,390
Where are you going?

300
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:53,470
To Castle Black. I'm a brother of the Night's Watch.

301
00:21:53,470 --> 00:21:55,140
- My brother, he's in the Night's-- - Shush.

302
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:57,170
- Who's your brother? - Doesn't matter.

303
00:22:06,590 --> 00:22:07,750
You're Jon's brother.

304
00:22:09,050 --> 00:22:10,700
The one who fell from the window.

305
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:11,640
No, I'm not.

306
00:22:13,150 --> 00:22:16,250
I've been around Ghost enough to know a direwolf when I see one.

307
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:19,410
And I've heard all about Hodor.

308
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:21,080
Hodor.

309
00:22:23,630 --> 00:22:25,960
I'd be dead if it wasn't for Jon.

310
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:28,420
If you're his brother, you're my brother, too.

311
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:31,060
And anything I can do to help you, I will.

312
00:22:31,830 --> 00:22:33,400
Take us north of the Wall.

313
00:22:38,850 --> 00:22:39,610
What?

314
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:41,760
Why in the world would you want to go--

315
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:43,940
I don't want to. I have to.

316
00:22:44,590 --> 00:22:45,790
How did you get through the Wall?

317
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,840
Does the well lead to an underground river?

318
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,970
Is that how you came here?

319
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:50,860
Come with us.

320
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:55,220
There are steps carved into the south side of the Wall.

321
00:22:55,230 --> 00:22:57,180
Hodor can carry you to the top.

322
00:22:57,180 --> 00:22:59,070
We'll walk straight to Castle Black.

323
00:22:59,430 --> 00:23:02,160
Come with us. There's nothing north but death.

324
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:05,090
If Jon is alive,

325
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:06,870
then Castle Black's where he'll be.

326
00:23:06,870 --> 00:23:08,520
It's the safest place for you.

327
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:11,560
There's nowhere safe any longer. You know that.

328
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:13,720
What I know is what I saw.

329
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:17,110
And if you saw it, too, you'd run the other way.

330
00:23:17,110 --> 00:23:19,900
You saw the white walkers and the army of the dead.

331
00:23:21,670 --> 00:23:22,790
How do you know all that?

332
00:23:23,130 --> 00:23:24,710
The Night's Watch can't stop them.

333
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:28,470
The kings of Westeros and all their armies can't stop them.

334
00:23:38,540 --> 00:23:40,170
But you're going to stop them?

335
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:41,730
Please, Sam.

336
00:23:43,310 --> 00:23:45,000
I have to go north.

337
00:23:46,890 --> 00:23:48,040
I have to.

338
00:24:16,890 --> 00:24:19,630
"Balon Greyjoy, Lord of the Iron Islands

339
00:24:19,630 --> 00:24:21,610
and invader of the North.

340
00:24:22,310 --> 00:24:24,000
I give you until the full moon

341
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:27,500
to order all ironborn scum out of the North

342
00:24:27,860 --> 00:24:30,400
and back to those shit-stained rocks

343
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:31,930
you call a home.

344
00:24:32,890 --> 00:24:35,060
On the first night of the full moon,

345
00:24:35,790 --> 00:24:37,930
I will hunt down every islander

346
00:24:37,930 --> 00:24:41,830
still in our lands and flay them living

347
00:24:42,770 --> 00:24:46,010
the way I flayed the 20 ironborn scum

348
00:24:46,020 --> 00:24:47,780
I found at Winterfell.

349
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:51,710
In the box you'll find a special gift--

350
00:24:52,710 --> 00:24:55,120
Theon's favorite toy.

351
00:24:56,020 --> 00:24:58,680
He cried when I took it away from him.

352
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:22,900
Leave the North now or more boxes will follow

353
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:25,360
with more Theon.

354
00:25:27,010 --> 00:25:28,420
Signed Ramsay Snow,

355
00:25:28,420 --> 00:25:29,970
natural-born son of Roose Bolton,

356
00:25:29,970 --> 00:25:32,960
Lord of the Dreadfort and Warden of the North."

357
00:25:35,980 --> 00:25:37,940
Get that out of my sight.

358
00:25:44,030 --> 00:25:47,220
Theon disobeyed my orders.

359
00:25:51,030 --> 00:25:52,890
The boy is a fool.

360
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:58,840
He cannot further the Greyjoy line.

361
00:26:00,490 --> 00:26:03,940
I will not give up the lands I have seized,

362
00:26:03,940 --> 00:26:05,950
the strongholds I have taken.

363
00:26:05,950 --> 00:26:07,580
Get this away from me.

364
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:10,180
He's your son.

365
00:26:10,470 --> 00:26:11,730
Son?

366
00:26:13,350 --> 00:26:15,270
He's not a man anymore.

367
00:26:16,030 --> 00:26:17,480
He's your son.

368
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:19,320
He's my brother.

369
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,250
He's a Greyjoy.

370
00:26:22,250 --> 00:26:23,610
Watch yourself.

371
00:26:24,710 --> 00:26:26,570
I've made my decision.

372
00:26:32,110 --> 00:26:33,360
And I've made mine.

373
00:26:37,080 --> 00:26:39,850
I'm going to pick the fastest ship in our fleet.

374
00:26:42,770 --> 00:26:46,160
I'm going to choose the 50 best killers on the Iron Islands.

375
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:47,600
Get those ropes!

376
00:26:48,430 --> 00:26:52,290
I'm going to sail up the Narrow Sea all the way to the Weeping Water.

377
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:56,220
I'm going to march on the Dreadfort.

378
00:26:57,190 --> 00:26:59,400
I'm going to find my little brother

379
00:27:00,260 --> 00:27:02,200
and I'm going to bring him home.

380
00:27:08,570 --> 00:27:09,460
What is it?

381
00:27:10,510 --> 00:27:11,710
Dragonglass.

382
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:13,130
We found them at the Fist.

383
00:27:13,920 --> 00:27:15,840
Someone buried them a long time ago.

384
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,910
Someone wanted us to find them.

385
00:27:20,020 --> 00:27:22,940
Why? What are they for?

386
00:27:27,740 --> 00:27:29,590
Killing white walkers.

387
00:27:29,590 --> 00:27:30,920
How do you know that?

388
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:33,330
The walker came for my baby.

389
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:35,350
And Sam...

390
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:39,060
But no one's killed a white walker in thousands of years.

391
00:27:39,060 --> 00:27:42,870
Well, I suppose someone had to be the first.

392
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:44,860
Take it, Hodor.

393
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:53,800
And the archer.

394
00:27:59,620 --> 00:28:00,610
I got lucky

395
00:28:01,990 --> 00:28:03,030
with one of them.

396
00:28:04,690 --> 00:28:05,810
There are more.

397
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:07,910
Many more.

398
00:28:09,390 --> 00:28:10,900
And for every one of them,

399
00:28:12,120 --> 00:28:13,110
the dead men,

400
00:28:14,970 --> 00:28:16,480
more than you could count.

401
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:21,770
I wish you'd come with us.

402
00:28:23,320 --> 00:28:24,490
I wish I could.

403
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:27,720
I really do.

404
00:29:15,870 --> 00:29:16,850
How are you keeping?

405
00:29:18,830 --> 00:29:19,800
Great.

406
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:21,890
Never better.

407
00:29:22,590 --> 00:29:23,960
It was just a bit of blood.

408
00:29:25,270 --> 00:29:26,410
I should have known.

409
00:29:27,290 --> 00:29:29,600
Every time a highborn asks my name, it's trouble.

410
00:29:31,060 --> 00:29:32,630
We're not really people to you, are we?

411
00:29:32,630 --> 00:29:34,500
Just a million different ways to get what you want.

412
00:29:34,500 --> 00:29:36,660
- I'm not a highborn. - She called you Ser.

413
00:29:37,500 --> 00:29:38,410
I heard it.

414
00:29:41,070 --> 00:29:43,100
A recent state of affairs.

415
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:49,310
I was born in Flea Bottom just like you.

416
00:29:50,980 --> 00:29:51,990
Sure, you were.

417
00:29:52,890 --> 00:29:54,730
You're my friend. You're here to help.

418
00:29:54,730 --> 00:29:56,550
I lived below the Street of Flour.

419
00:29:56,990 --> 00:29:57,890
How far below?

420
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,110
How close to the Red Keep were you?

421
00:30:01,750 --> 00:30:04,590
The shit that poured from their privy pipes

422
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:07,650
flowed down the side of Aegon's Hill

423
00:30:08,340 --> 00:30:11,560
along Tanner's Row and right in front of my front door

424
00:30:12,100 --> 00:30:13,880
- on Gin Alley. - Gin Alley.

425
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:18,320
The Street of Steel,

426
00:30:19,060 --> 00:30:21,610
with your armor and your knights? Pfft.

427
00:30:22,270 --> 00:30:23,980
You lived in the fancy part of town.

428
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:30,120
And here we are now.

429
00:30:31,610 --> 00:30:34,400
Two boys from Flea Bottom in the castle of a king.

430
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:37,160
Yeah, we've come a long way.

431
00:30:38,500 --> 00:30:40,160
We're all the same, really.

432
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:43,310
She went to great pains to point that out to me.

433
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:46,180
If you mistrust fancy people so much,

434
00:30:46,180 --> 00:30:48,290
why were you in such a hurry to trust her?

435
00:30:50,700 --> 00:30:51,690
You're me.

436
00:30:53,470 --> 00:30:54,800
Never been with a woman.

437
00:30:55,180 --> 00:30:57,220
Never talked to a woman, really.

438
00:30:57,630 --> 00:30:59,110
And then she comes at you...

439
00:31:00,070 --> 00:31:01,710
big words, no clothes.

440
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:03,520
What would you have done?

441
00:31:05,630 --> 00:31:08,640
She does know her way around a man's head, I'll give her that.

442
00:31:15,210 --> 00:31:16,560
So how'd you become a lord?

443
00:31:17,470 --> 00:31:19,440
Oh, that's a long story.

444
00:31:19,440 --> 00:31:22,320
Better not, then. I'm a bit busy.

445
00:31:25,930 --> 00:31:27,520
Many years ago I helped King Stannis

446
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:29,040
out of a difficult situation.

447
00:31:30,430 --> 00:31:32,240
He rewarded me with a lordship.

448
00:31:33,740 --> 00:31:35,380
And this.

449
00:31:37,740 --> 00:31:38,650
You see?

450
00:31:40,020 --> 00:31:41,390
Highborns.

451
00:31:45,610 --> 00:31:46,970
I didn't want to be a lord.

452
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:49,890
I nearly didn't accept.

453
00:31:50,460 --> 00:31:51,430
Why did you?

454
00:31:51,430 --> 00:31:52,670
I did it for my son.

455
00:31:54,650 --> 00:31:56,810
I didn't want him to step over a river of shit

456
00:31:56,810 --> 00:31:58,910
every time he stepped through his front door.

457
00:32:01,140 --> 00:32:02,910
I wanted him to have a better life.

458
00:32:05,590 --> 00:32:06,460
Does he?

459
00:32:08,230 --> 00:32:09,490
He's dead.

460
00:32:15,660 --> 00:32:16,750
How'd he die?

461
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:19,760
Following me.

462
00:32:31,090 --> 00:32:33,530
When did you come to this strange country?

463
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:37,620
When I was 13.

464
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:39,290
You were only a child.

465
00:32:40,760 --> 00:32:43,320
I stopped being a child when I was nine.

466
00:32:43,990 --> 00:32:45,820
My mother made sure of that.

467
00:32:47,930 --> 00:32:49,450
You've been a good influence

468
00:32:49,450 --> 00:32:51,390
on our mutual friend, you know.

469
00:32:51,960 --> 00:32:53,890
He used to drink from sundown to sunup,

470
00:32:53,890 --> 00:32:55,540
visit three brothels a night,

471
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:57,470
gamble away his father's money.

472
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:00,390
Now it's just the drinking.

473
00:33:01,370 --> 00:33:03,500
And now I'm his wife's servant.

474
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:05,490
I brush her hair and clip her nails

475
00:33:05,490 --> 00:33:06,880
and empty her chamber pot.

476
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:08,330
She is a sweet young thing.

477
00:33:08,330 --> 00:33:09,820
None of this is her fault.

478
00:33:09,990 --> 00:33:12,700
I love that girl. I would kill for her.

479
00:33:13,130 --> 00:33:14,950
Do you think that makes it easier for me?

480
00:33:14,950 --> 00:33:17,250
No, I expect not.

481
00:33:19,840 --> 00:33:23,820
She's young and she's beautiful and highborn.

482
00:33:24,020 --> 00:33:25,440
We break bread with them,

483
00:33:25,630 --> 00:33:27,370
but that doesn't make us family.

484
00:33:28,630 --> 00:33:29,620
We've learned their language,

485
00:33:29,620 --> 00:33:31,880
but we'll never be their countrymen.

486
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:36,660
If you let yourself believe

487
00:33:37,270 --> 00:33:39,310
that a foreign girl with no name

488
00:33:39,310 --> 00:33:41,670
could spend her life with the son of Tywin Lannister--

489
00:33:41,670 --> 00:33:44,110
- I have a name. - You have one name.

490
00:33:44,860 --> 00:33:45,960
As do I.

491
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:48,610
Here only the family name matters.

492
00:33:49,230 --> 00:33:50,970
What do you want from me, Lord Varys?

493
00:33:55,040 --> 00:33:56,190
Diamonds.

494
00:33:57,010 --> 00:33:59,630
I'd tell you to beware carrying so much wealth,

495
00:33:59,630 --> 00:34:02,040
but you know how to protect yourself.

496
00:34:02,850 --> 00:34:04,450
Get on one of those ships.

497
00:34:04,870 --> 00:34:07,700
Sail to Pentos or Lys or Myr.

498
00:34:08,200 --> 00:34:10,530
You can buy a house with these diamonds,

499
00:34:11,020 --> 00:34:12,870
a very large house.

500
00:34:12,870 --> 00:34:14,330
Hire servants.

501
00:34:14,770 --> 00:34:15,890
Start a new life,

502
00:34:15,890 --> 00:34:18,650
a good life, far from here.

503
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:21,610
The mysterious foreign beauty.

504
00:34:21,610 --> 00:34:23,770
You'll have suitors lining up.

505
00:34:24,340 --> 00:34:25,910
Why do you want me to leave?

506
00:34:26,170 --> 00:34:28,730
Tyrion Lannister is one of the few people alive

507
00:34:28,730 --> 00:34:30,650
who could make this country a better place.

508
00:34:30,650 --> 00:34:32,450
He has the mind for it, he has the will,

509
00:34:32,450 --> 00:34:33,810
he has the right last name.

510
00:34:33,810 --> 00:34:34,730
And you--

511
00:34:36,070 --> 00:34:38,960
you are a complication.

512
00:34:40,700 --> 00:34:42,920
I know you love him.

513
00:34:43,180 --> 00:34:46,550
And I know it's true love not bought by gold and silver.

514
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:48,840
I'm not asking you to leave him for money.

515
00:34:49,620 --> 00:34:51,670
I'm asking you to leave

516
00:34:51,670 --> 00:34:56,510
because your presence in the capital endangers him.

517
00:34:58,110 --> 00:35:00,740
This will never be your home, my lady.

518
00:35:00,930 --> 00:35:04,790
Find a true home somewhere far from here...

519
00:35:06,090 --> 00:35:08,250
while there's still time.

520
00:35:09,520 --> 00:35:10,770
Lord Varys.

521
00:35:15,620 --> 00:35:18,360
If he wants me to leave, he can tell me himself.

522
00:35:27,950 --> 00:35:29,160
Keep up.

523
00:35:29,970 --> 00:35:31,650
I don't think I can, my lord.

524
00:35:34,130 --> 00:35:36,370
It's not easy being drunk all the time.

525
00:35:38,170 --> 00:35:40,750
Everyone would do it if it were easy.

526
00:35:44,020 --> 00:35:45,020
Leave.

527
00:35:54,760 --> 00:35:57,810
So, enjoying married life?

528
00:36:01,250 --> 00:36:04,650
An unhappy wife is a wine merchant's best friend.

529
00:36:05,970 --> 00:36:07,700
She doesn't deserve this.

530
00:36:07,700 --> 00:36:08,830
Deserve?

531
00:36:09,760 --> 00:36:11,140
Be careful with that.

532
00:36:12,710 --> 00:36:15,170
Start trying to work out who deserves what

533
00:36:15,580 --> 00:36:18,070
and before long you'll spend the rest of your days

534
00:36:18,070 --> 00:36:21,330
weeping for each and every person in the world.

535
00:36:21,330 --> 00:36:24,480
There's nothing worse than a late-blooming philosopher.

536
00:36:26,230 --> 00:36:28,900
Will you be facing your marriage to Ser Loras

537
00:36:28,900 --> 00:36:31,590
with the same philosophical spirit?

538
00:36:31,590 --> 00:36:33,300
I won't be marrying Ser Loras.

539
00:36:33,300 --> 00:36:36,080
I seem to remember saying something similar

540
00:36:36,080 --> 00:36:37,820
about my own marriage.

541
00:36:38,330 --> 00:36:39,550
You're not me.

542
00:36:41,610 --> 00:36:43,470
You want to make things better for Sansa?

543
00:36:43,470 --> 00:36:44,950
Give her a child.

544
00:36:45,230 --> 00:36:47,020
So you can tell father it was you

545
00:36:47,630 --> 00:36:49,360
who finally talked me into it?

546
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:52,130
So she can have some happiness in her life.

547
00:36:52,950 --> 00:36:54,450
You have children.

548
00:36:54,980 --> 00:36:57,210
How happy would you say you are?

549
00:37:00,740 --> 00:37:01,930
Not very.

550
00:37:05,210 --> 00:37:07,300
But if it weren't for my children,

551
00:37:07,300 --> 00:37:09,940
I'd have thrown myself from the highest window in the Red Keep.

552
00:37:12,090 --> 00:37:13,800
They're the reason I'm alive.

553
00:37:14,880 --> 00:37:15,960
Even Joffrey?

554
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:18,990
Even Joffrey.

555
00:37:23,330 --> 00:37:25,160
He was all I had once.

556
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:27,660
Before Myrcella was born.

557
00:37:31,880 --> 00:37:35,640
I used to spend hours looking at him.

558
00:37:37,050 --> 00:37:38,480
His wisps of hair.

559
00:37:40,250 --> 00:37:42,330
His tiny little hands and feet.

560
00:37:43,940 --> 00:37:45,730
He was such a jolly little fellow.

561
00:37:49,430 --> 00:37:52,370
You always hear the terrible ones were terrible babies.

562
00:37:52,640 --> 00:37:55,170
"We should have known. Even then we should have known."

563
00:37:55,170 --> 00:37:56,550
It's nonsense.

564
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:01,350
Whenever he was with me, he was happy.

565
00:38:06,140 --> 00:38:07,390
And no one can take that away from me,

566
00:38:07,390 --> 00:38:08,760
not even Joffrey--

567
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:11,210
how it feels to have someone.

568
00:38:12,910 --> 00:38:14,370
Someone of your own.

569
00:38:25,310 --> 00:38:26,900
How long does it go on?

570
00:38:30,460 --> 00:38:32,510
Until we've dealt with all our enemies.

571
00:38:34,700 --> 00:38:36,530
Every time we deal with an enemy,

572
00:38:37,340 --> 00:38:39,180
we create two more.

573
00:38:41,100 --> 00:38:43,590
Then I suppose it will go on for quite a long time.

574
00:38:49,040 --> 00:38:51,410
I'm telling you, that's what she did.

575
00:38:55,070 --> 00:38:56,910
Sounded like a cow in heat.

576
00:38:56,910 --> 00:38:59,040
- Aye, not for long. - That's right.

577
00:38:59,240 --> 00:39:01,300
Black Walder shut her up right quick.

578
00:39:01,660 --> 00:39:04,740
None of the Starks had much to say about the end of that meal.

579
00:39:04,740 --> 00:39:05,880
I'll tell you what, though.

580
00:39:06,340 --> 00:39:07,190
The hardest thing was

581
00:39:07,190 --> 00:39:09,170
getting that wolf's head to stay on the body.

582
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:12,350
- You sewed it on? - I did.

583
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:15,310
I bet there were 1,000 men claiming they were the one.

584
00:39:15,310 --> 00:39:16,650
It was me.

585
00:39:17,180 --> 00:39:19,850
And Malcolm and Talbott.

586
00:39:20,750 --> 00:39:22,760
Well, the thing was so heavy, it fell off the first time.

587
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:24,710
Took the skin right with it.

588
00:39:24,710 --> 00:39:27,660
What we ended up having to do was hook the needle

589
00:39:27,660 --> 00:39:29,220
right under the collarbone.

590
00:39:29,220 --> 00:39:31,360
Give it a nice firm mooring and--

591
00:39:35,250 --> 00:39:36,450
What do you want?

592
00:39:36,640 --> 00:39:39,390
- Mind if I keep warm? - Fuck off.

593
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:41,150
But I'm hungry.

594
00:39:42,300 --> 00:39:45,980
Does fuck off mean something different where you're from?

595
00:39:45,980 --> 00:39:47,310
I've got money.

596
00:39:52,190 --> 00:39:53,590
What kind of coin is that?

597
00:39:53,930 --> 00:39:55,570
It's worth a lot.

598
00:39:58,210 --> 00:39:59,360
Sorry.

599
00:40:00,470 --> 00:40:01,670
Little shit.

600
00:40:06,580 --> 00:40:07,490
Fool!

601
00:40:23,270 --> 00:40:25,150
Where did you get the knife?

602
00:40:26,120 --> 00:40:27,000
From you.

603
00:40:31,020 --> 00:40:32,780
Is that the first man you've killed?

604
00:40:33,530 --> 00:40:34,780
The first man.

605
00:40:36,860 --> 00:40:38,800
Next time you're going to do something like that,

606
00:40:39,370 --> 00:40:40,780
tell me first.

607
00:40:53,290 --> 00:40:54,810
Valar morghulis.

608
00:41:24,770 --> 00:41:27,080
Ygritte, you know I didn't have a choice.

609
00:41:30,690 --> 00:41:32,520
You always knew who I was,

610
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,370
what I am.

611
00:41:37,880 --> 00:41:39,420
I have to go home now.

612
00:41:42,470 --> 00:41:44,170
I know you won't hurt me.

613
00:41:46,340 --> 00:41:48,030
You know nothing, Jon Snow.

614
00:41:52,290 --> 00:41:53,700
I do know some things.

615
00:41:55,940 --> 00:41:57,230
I know I love you.

616
00:42:00,200 --> 00:42:01,580
I know you love me.

617
00:42:04,970 --> 00:42:06,630
But I have to go home now.

618
00:42:48,500 --> 00:42:50,680
I know how this must look.

619
00:42:54,420 --> 00:42:56,500
- What I meant was-- - I swear to you, my lord--

620
00:42:56,500 --> 00:42:57,950
I'm not a lord, my dear.

621
00:42:59,400 --> 00:43:01,350
Not for many, many years.

622
00:43:02,230 --> 00:43:04,870
Every man who joins the Night's Watch

623
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:08,840
renounces all former titles.

624
00:43:11,020 --> 00:43:12,340
Among other things.

625
00:43:16,410 --> 00:43:17,490
What is your name?

626
00:43:18,310 --> 00:43:19,100
Gilly.

627
00:43:19,300 --> 00:43:22,630
Ah, for the gillyflower.

628
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:24,890
Lovely.

629
00:43:25,330 --> 00:43:26,440
Yes, my--

630
00:43:29,530 --> 00:43:30,630
Maester.

631
00:43:31,830 --> 00:43:33,000
Master.

632
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:34,380
Maester.

633
00:43:35,410 --> 00:43:37,390
And the child?

634
00:43:38,950 --> 00:43:40,660
She hasn't chosen a name yet.

635
00:43:41,310 --> 00:43:42,620
His name is Sam.

636
00:43:46,920 --> 00:43:47,830
Tarly...

637
00:43:49,130 --> 00:43:52,050
do you remember the oath you swore

638
00:43:53,070 --> 00:43:54,980
when you joined this order?

639
00:43:55,610 --> 00:43:58,060
He's not my child, Maester Aemon.

640
00:43:59,670 --> 00:44:01,600
She's one of Craster's wives.

641
00:44:06,440 --> 00:44:09,650
I remember every word of the oath.

642
00:44:11,020 --> 00:44:13,750
Night gathers and my watch begins.

643
00:44:14,230 --> 00:44:17,330
I am the shield that guards the realms of men.

644
00:44:19,840 --> 00:44:21,630
The realms of men.

645
00:44:24,120 --> 00:44:26,320
That means her as well as us.

646
00:44:27,310 --> 00:44:30,350
We didn't build 500 miles of ice walls

647
00:44:30,350 --> 00:44:32,700
700 feet high to keep out men.

648
00:44:35,340 --> 00:44:37,280
The night is gathering, Maester Aemon.

649
00:44:37,280 --> 00:44:38,290
I've seen it.

650
00:44:39,680 --> 00:44:41,200
It's coming for all of us.

651
00:44:44,660 --> 00:44:47,770
Gilly, you and your son

652
00:44:48,330 --> 00:44:50,880
will be our guests for the time being.

653
00:44:51,580 --> 00:44:55,230
We certainly cannot send you back

654
00:44:56,330 --> 00:44:57,540
beyond the Wall.

655
00:44:58,610 --> 00:44:59,660
Thank you...

656
00:45:00,540 --> 00:45:01,790
Maester.

657
00:45:02,870 --> 00:45:04,750
I can cook and clean and I can--

658
00:45:04,750 --> 00:45:05,490
Good.

659
00:45:06,450 --> 00:45:11,020
Samwell, fetch a quill and inkwell.

660
00:45:15,490 --> 00:45:18,950
I hope your penmanship is better than your swordplay.

661
00:45:19,550 --> 00:45:20,780
Miles better.

662
00:45:22,690 --> 00:45:26,420
We had 44 ravens at last count.

663
00:45:27,070 --> 00:45:29,010
Make sure they're all fed.

664
00:45:30,210 --> 00:45:32,230
Every one of them flies tonight.

665
00:45:42,460 --> 00:45:47,080
"To His Grace king Stannis Baratheon.

666
00:45:49,230 --> 00:45:51,610
Invaded-- inv-- invit-- invited

667
00:45:52,290 --> 00:45:55,500
to the name day celebration

668
00:45:55,810 --> 00:46:00,660
for Rylene Florent

669
00:46:01,330 --> 00:46:03,450
on the first nigit--"

670
00:46:03,850 --> 00:46:04,920
Night.

671
00:46:05,330 --> 00:46:07,620
"First night of the full moon."

672
00:46:07,620 --> 00:46:09,030
Why is there a G in night?

673
00:46:09,030 --> 00:46:10,810
I don't know. There just is.

674
00:46:12,600 --> 00:46:14,080
Well, your father's not going to go to that.

675
00:46:15,790 --> 00:46:18,260
My books are better than these boring scrolls.

676
00:46:18,260 --> 00:46:20,410
You could read about Balerion the Dread.

677
00:46:20,410 --> 00:46:23,820
They say you can still see his skull in the dungeons beneath the Red Keep.

678
00:46:24,840 --> 00:46:26,160
I'd like to see that someday.

679
00:46:26,460 --> 00:46:29,050
I've been trying to stay out of those dungeons my whole life.

680
00:46:30,460 --> 00:46:33,000
"His fangs were as long as bastard swords."

681
00:46:34,690 --> 00:46:36,270
Aye, old Balerion's definitely better

682
00:46:36,270 --> 00:46:38,620
than anything your cousin Rylene's got on offer.

683
00:46:39,980 --> 00:46:42,050
But now that I'm your father's Hand again,

684
00:46:42,300 --> 00:46:44,040
I have to keep him informed.

685
00:46:45,500 --> 00:46:47,730
The king does not have time for this drudgery.

686
00:46:50,040 --> 00:46:53,880
"To all the lords and knobble men of Westeros."

687
00:46:53,880 --> 00:46:56,280
- Noblemen. - "Noblemen of Westeros,

688
00:46:57,580 --> 00:47:00,790
the Nig-- the Night's Watch...

689
00:47:04,420 --> 00:47:05,570
implores..."

690
00:47:06,780 --> 00:47:07,870
What is it?

691
00:47:12,990 --> 00:47:14,500
Why are they ringing the bells?

692
00:47:15,310 --> 00:47:16,710
Are we being attacked?

693
00:47:17,260 --> 00:47:18,210
Stay here.

694
00:47:19,610 --> 00:47:20,580
Bar the door.

695
00:47:39,980 --> 00:47:42,050
The usurper Robb Stark is dead.

696
00:47:42,240 --> 00:47:44,210
Betrayed by his bannerman.

697
00:47:46,050 --> 00:47:49,190
And you take credit because you dropped a leech into the fire?

698
00:47:49,190 --> 00:47:50,460
I take no credit.

699
00:47:51,270 --> 00:47:53,570
I have faith and my faith has been rewarded.

700
00:47:57,040 --> 00:48:01,220
Your Grace, the world has got so far bent.

701
00:48:01,790 --> 00:48:04,180
I've seen things crawl out of nightmares,

702
00:48:04,180 --> 00:48:05,650
but my eyes were open.

703
00:48:06,110 --> 00:48:07,220
I don't know if Robb Stark

704
00:48:07,220 --> 00:48:08,850
died because of the Red Woman's sorcery

705
00:48:08,850 --> 00:48:10,990
or because at war men die all the time,

706
00:48:10,990 --> 00:48:14,140
but I do know that uniting the Seven Kingdoms

707
00:48:14,140 --> 00:48:16,120
with blood magic is wrong.

708
00:48:16,120 --> 00:48:17,100
It is evil.

709
00:48:17,100 --> 00:48:19,040
And you are not an evil man.

710
00:48:19,220 --> 00:48:22,400
Do you know who had this table carved and painted, Ser Davos?

711
00:48:23,310 --> 00:48:24,380
Aegon Targaryen.

712
00:48:24,380 --> 00:48:26,960
And do you know how Aegon Targaryen conquered Westeros?

713
00:48:26,960 --> 00:48:29,100
On the back of his dragon Balerion the Dread.

714
00:48:29,690 --> 00:48:33,020
He had a smaller fleet than the kings he faced

715
00:48:33,020 --> 00:48:35,660
and a smaller army, but he had three dragons.

716
00:48:35,660 --> 00:48:38,030
Dragons are magic, Ser Davos.

717
00:48:38,410 --> 00:48:41,100
My enemies have made my kingdom bleed.

718
00:48:43,190 --> 00:48:44,610
I will not forget that.

719
00:48:46,340 --> 00:48:47,730
I will not forgive that.

720
00:48:49,620 --> 00:48:53,560
I will punish them with any arms at my disposal.

721
00:48:53,970 --> 00:48:56,070
You do not need to burn the boy.

722
00:48:57,790 --> 00:48:59,280
If what you say is true,

723
00:49:00,520 --> 00:49:02,930
a drop of his blood killed Robb Stark--

724
00:49:02,930 --> 00:49:05,410
And our king is still no closer to the Iron Throne.

725
00:49:08,580 --> 00:49:11,290
A great gift requires a great sacrifice.

726
00:49:28,740 --> 00:49:29,950
His name is Gendry.

727
00:49:31,170 --> 00:49:32,260
He's a good lad.

728
00:49:33,660 --> 00:49:35,800
A poor lad from Flea Bottom

729
00:49:36,020 --> 00:49:38,210
who happens to be your nephew.

730
00:49:43,680 --> 00:49:46,980
What is the life of one bastard boy against a kingdom?

731
00:49:49,190 --> 00:49:50,160
Everything.

732
00:49:51,820 --> 00:49:52,970
The boy must die.

733
00:50:01,490 --> 00:50:02,930
- What are you doing? - You're leaving.

734
00:50:04,760 --> 00:50:06,090
Is this some kind of trick?

735
00:50:06,090 --> 00:50:07,820
Yes, but not on you.

736
00:50:12,950 --> 00:50:15,690
Aim for that star. Don't stop.

737
00:50:15,690 --> 00:50:17,760
There's bread and water. Go slow with it.

738
00:50:18,300 --> 00:50:19,370
If you finish it off,

739
00:50:20,460 --> 00:50:22,250
no matter how thirsty you get,

740
00:50:23,170 --> 00:50:25,180
don't drink seawater.

741
00:50:25,570 --> 00:50:26,990
I know not to drink seawater.

742
00:50:26,990 --> 00:50:30,440
Row for a full day and night and you'll reach Rook's Rest.

743
00:50:31,010 --> 00:50:33,740
You'll want to stop there. Don't. She'll find you.

744
00:50:33,950 --> 00:50:34,890
Where should I go?

745
00:50:34,890 --> 00:50:36,280
You must keep the coast on your left side

746
00:50:36,280 --> 00:50:37,780
until you reach King's Landing.

747
00:50:37,980 --> 00:50:39,360
The gold cloaks are looking for me.

748
00:50:39,960 --> 00:50:41,490
They were looking for me for 20 years.

749
00:50:41,490 --> 00:50:43,280
- Do they know your face? - No.

750
00:50:43,280 --> 00:50:44,800
I'd worry more about the Red Woman.

751
00:50:52,560 --> 00:50:53,630
The other way.

752
00:50:58,420 --> 00:51:00,140
You ever been in a boat before?

753
00:51:01,200 --> 00:51:01,740
No.

754
00:51:01,910 --> 00:51:02,980
You know how to swim?

755
00:51:03,870 --> 00:51:04,470
No.

756
00:51:04,810 --> 00:51:05,830
Don't fall out.

757
00:51:06,450 --> 00:51:07,220
Go on.

758
00:51:10,810 --> 00:51:11,870
Why are you doing this?

759
00:51:12,080 --> 00:51:13,160
Because it's right.

760
00:51:14,380 --> 00:51:15,990
And because I'm a slow learner.

761
00:51:19,250 --> 00:51:22,360
When you get to Flea Bottom, have a bowl of brown for me.

762
00:51:27,270 --> 00:51:28,890
Horse approaching!

763
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:32,110
Halt! Halt!

764
00:51:49,970 --> 00:51:51,650
Jon! Jon!

765
00:51:52,080 --> 00:51:53,210
Jon, it's us.

766
00:51:53,440 --> 00:51:54,840
I don't think he can see us.

767
00:51:59,920 --> 00:52:00,830
Pyp?

768
00:52:04,300 --> 00:52:05,250
Sam?

769
00:52:05,250 --> 00:52:08,330
Hush, now. You're home.

770
00:52:10,190 --> 00:52:12,420
Carry him inside. Gently.

771
00:52:38,720 --> 00:52:39,530
Out of the way.

772
00:52:41,140 --> 00:52:42,540
Step aside, country boy.

773
00:52:42,540 --> 00:52:43,610
People working here.

774
00:53:29,840 --> 00:53:31,010
Cersei.

775
00:53:50,300 --> 00:53:51,490
You don't deny it?

776
00:53:53,120 --> 00:53:53,890
No.

777
00:53:55,300 --> 00:53:56,550
I let him go.

778
00:53:57,760 --> 00:54:00,150
Your mercy saved the boy's life.

779
00:54:01,000 --> 00:54:02,220
You feel good about that?

780
00:54:02,220 --> 00:54:03,740
Aye, I do.

781
00:54:04,670 --> 00:54:06,190
You saved one innocent.

782
00:54:06,750 --> 00:54:09,840
How many tens of thousands have you doomed?

783
00:54:13,520 --> 00:54:15,720
There has got to be another way.

784
00:54:15,930 --> 00:54:17,140
What other way?!

785
00:54:17,140 --> 00:54:19,100
Tell us about this other way.

786
00:54:19,100 --> 00:54:20,350
I don't know, Your Grace.

787
00:54:21,390 --> 00:54:23,080
I can't see the future in the fire.

788
00:54:27,980 --> 00:54:29,680
Very well, Ser Davos Seaworth.

789
00:54:31,330 --> 00:54:33,530
I, Stannis of the House Baratheon,

790
00:54:33,530 --> 00:54:36,080
First of My Name, Rightful King of the Andals and the First Men,

791
00:54:36,080 --> 00:54:38,070
- sentence you to die. - I understand.

792
00:54:38,450 --> 00:54:40,360
But since you haven't yet unnamed me Hand of the King,

793
00:54:40,360 --> 00:54:42,820
it is my duty to advise you against it.

794
00:54:43,270 --> 00:54:45,100
- You're gonna need me. - Take him away.

795
00:54:47,350 --> 00:54:48,390
Why am I gonna need you?

796
00:54:53,020 --> 00:54:53,850
My king.

797
00:54:58,550 --> 00:55:00,650
It's from Maester Aemon of the Night's Watch.

798
00:55:01,000 --> 00:55:02,630
Their Lord Commander is dead.

799
00:55:02,630 --> 00:55:05,310
Took a ranging party north and never made it back.

800
00:55:05,530 --> 00:55:07,000
One lad did, though.

801
00:55:07,680 --> 00:55:09,770
What he saw beyond the Wall--

802
00:55:10,510 --> 00:55:12,550
it's coming for all of us.

803
00:55:26,980 --> 00:55:28,220
When did you learn to read?

804
00:55:28,890 --> 00:55:30,190
Matthos taught me before he died

805
00:55:30,190 --> 00:55:32,170
so I could be of better service to you.

806
00:55:39,980 --> 00:55:42,830
This War of Five Kings means nothing.

807
00:55:44,350 --> 00:55:46,950
The true war lies to the north, my king.

808
00:55:48,920 --> 00:55:50,550
Death marches on the Wall.

809
00:55:52,110 --> 00:55:53,670
Only you can stop him.

810
00:55:54,030 --> 00:55:55,440
You can't stop him alone.

811
00:55:56,230 --> 00:55:57,970
You need someone to rebuild your army for you,

812
00:55:58,810 --> 00:56:01,200
someone to convince this lord and that lord to fight for you,

813
00:56:01,200 --> 00:56:03,840
to bring sellswords and pirates to your side.

814
00:56:03,840 --> 00:56:05,010
I've made my decision.

815
00:56:07,470 --> 00:56:10,370
He's right. You need him.

816
00:56:10,530 --> 00:56:12,970
He has a part to play in the war to come.

817
00:56:22,400 --> 00:56:23,790
You see, Ser Davos?

818
00:56:24,820 --> 00:56:27,820
You've been saved by that fire god you like to mock.

819
00:56:31,630 --> 00:56:33,170
You're in his army now.

820
00:56:56,960 --> 00:56:58,330
They will come, Your Grace.

821
00:56:59,250 --> 00:57:00,700
When they're ready.

822
00:57:01,200 --> 00:57:03,090
Perhaps they didn't want to be conquered.

823
00:57:03,490 --> 00:57:04,790
You didn't conquer them.

824
00:57:05,610 --> 00:57:07,130
You liberated them.

825
00:57:08,580 --> 00:57:10,660
People learn to love their chains.

826
00:58:15,270 --> 00:58:16,130
No.

827
00:58:55,430 --> 00:58:57,200
- Mhysa! - Mhysa!

828
00:58:57,420 --> 00:58:59,260
Mhysa! Mhysa!

829
00:58:59,850 --> 00:59:02,640
Mhysa! Mhysa! Mhysa!

830
00:59:03,600 --> 00:59:04,610
What does it mean?

831
00:59:05,750 --> 00:59:07,470
It is old Ghiscari, khaleesi.

832
00:59:08,650 --> 00:59:10,650
It means "Mother."

833
00:59:16,380 --> 00:59:17,530
It's all right.

834
00:59:19,090 --> 00:59:20,540
These people won't hurt me.

835
00:59:23,300 --> 00:59:25,970
Mhysa! Mhysa!

836
01:00:14,740 --> 01:00:19,910
Mhysa.

837
01:00:30,100 --> 01:00:32,710
Mhysa! Mhysa! Mhysa!

